    "summary": "Man’s gown (boubou, tobe), hand-woven from hand-spun cotton dyed in indigo. The body is formed of 43 narrow strips hand-sewn together along the selvedges vertically, while the sleeves are sewn horizontally. At the front is a large pocket. Both the front and the back are extensively embroidered with hand-sewn decoration in white, yellow, green, blue and red imported European cotton thread using some buttonhole eyelet stitching. These form geometrical patterns of spirals, zig-zags, strips and circles.",
